# ReArc engine — pinned upstream Chromium version.
#
# This file is the single source of truth for which upstream Chromium
# release the ReArc engine is built from. engine/scripts/fetch.sh reads
# the last non-comment line of this file and syncs the checkout at
# engine/chromium/ to that exact tag.
#
# BUMP PROCEDURE (do all steps in one commit):
#   1. Pick a new version from the Chrome stable channel
#      (see https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/releases?platform=Mac).
#      Prefer small increments (one or two milestones at a time) — the
#      patch overlay is rebased by hand and large jumps multiply
#      conflicts.
#   2. Replace the version line below with the new full version
#      (MAJOR.MINOR.BUILD.PATCH, matching the upstream git tag exactly).
#   3. Run engine/scripts/fetch.sh to sync engine/chromium/ to the tag.
#   4. Rebase the patch overlay following the checklist in
#      engine/patches/README.md. Refresh any patch that fails to apply
#      and commit the refreshed patches alongside this file.
#   5. Run engine/scripts/build.sh and smoke-test shell integration
#      (tab create/navigate/close, favicon+title events, media state).
#   6. Update engine/docs/IPC-CONTRACT.md if any engine behavior the
#      shell depends on changed.
#
# NOTE: the IPC contract version is versioned independently of this pin.
# A Chromium bump does not imply an IPC contract bump.
